From: DIR-842 R1 port
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: rtl8365mb: widen the indirect-access poll timeout

Waiting for the indirect PHY access to complete is given 100us. Each poll is
itself a register access, and over the bit-banged SMI transport a single access
is tens of microseconds of software bit toggling, so the whole budget can expire
inside one iteration whenever the CPU is busy with something else.

Observed on an RTL8197F board driving this switch over bit-banged SMI: sustained
traffic produces a burst of "failed to read PHY.. -ETIMEDOUT", after which
phylink reports every port down and they do not come back.

Widen the timeout to 10ms. On a real MDIO controller the loop still exits on its
first read, so nothing changes there.

--- a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_main.c	2026-09-02 14:52:01.748198795 -0300
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_main.c	2026-09-02 14:52:01.756199069 -0300
@@ -864,9 +864,16 @@
 {
 	u32 val;
 
+	/*
+	 * Every poll here is itself a register access, and on the bit-banged SMI
+	 * transport one of those takes tens of microseconds of software toggling
+	 * -- so a 100us budget can expire inside a single iteration once the CPU
+	 * is busy elsewhere. Allow enough time for the slow transport; on a real
+	 * MDIO controller the loop still exits on the first read.
+	 */
 	return regmap_read_poll_timeout(priv->map_nolock,
 					RTL8365MB_INDIRECT_ACCESS_STATUS_REG,
-					val, !val, 10, 100);
+					val, !val, 10, 10000);
 }
 
 static int rtl8365mb_phy_ocp_prepare(struct realtek_priv *priv, int phy,
